Katia Gil Guzman (OpenAI) challenges you to build more ambitious UIs.

Hi Sayantan,

We partnered with OpenAI to make our new Codex course free for everyone ( h=
ttps://master.dev/courses/codex/?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dcourse-rel=
ease&utm_campaign=3Dcodex&code=3Dlearncodex ). No subscription, no trial.

Katia Gil Guzman, from OpenAI, has always loved building UIs. Agentic codin=
g tools like Codex let her experiment and innovate freely, like in this pro=
ject from the course:

But this UI wasn't one-shotted. Version 1 was a good start, but needed work=
. And that's Katia's message throughout this whole course. You, as the engi=
neer, know what "done" looks like. So she wants to better equip you with pr=
actical workflows in Codex to help get you there.

This course is a rare opportunity to learn directly from the Codex team. An=
d it's 100% free ( https://master.dev/courses/codex/?utm_source=3Demail&utm=
_medium=3Dcourse-release&utm_campaign=3Dcodex&code=3Dlearncodex ).

---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
Agentic Frontend Development with Codex ( https://master.dev/courses/codex/=
?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dcourse-release&utm_campaign=3Dcodex&code=
=3Dlearncodex )
---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----

Leverage the power of Codex in your frontend development workflows. Plan, d=
ebug, and reimagine modern interfaces while keeping control over the qualit=
y, accessibility, and UI polish.

Katia Gil Guzman sitting next to a student while teaching her how to use Co=
dex ( https://master.dev/courses/codex/?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dcou=
rse-release&utm_campaign=3Dcodex&code=3Dlearncodex )

*What you'll walk away with:*

* Discover where Codex fits in your workflow: From ideation and prototyping=
, to building, debugging, and polishing rich frontend experiences.
* Configured for your codebase: Gain best-practices for your Agents.md file=
s and create skills and plugins to save time and share repeatable tasks.
* Define what done means: Leverage goal settings to better direct the AI an=
d establish an iterative and reliable testing process.
* Deploy directly from Codex: Collaborate with your team through GitHub PRs=
 or publish frontend applications to ChatGPT Sites.
* Everything can be interactive: Build "living frontends" that adapt on the=
 fly and can be reshaped by anyone on the team.

Start learning Codex for free ( https://master.dev/courses/codex/?utm_sourc=
e=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dcourse-release&utm_campaign=3Dcodex&code=3Dlearncode=
x ) !

Happy learning!

